  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) achieved only 48.5% accuracy, a weak baseline that leaves major uncertainty about which modality or representation will drive performance. Question: Does the image modality carry useful signal for this task? config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) is the cleanest single-modality comparison to config_001—same profile setting (singleprofile), no aggregation or fusion needed—so any accuracy difference can be attributed primarily to the modality switch. Why this is the best next step: With 8 experiments remaining, knowing whether image features are informative at all is the highest-leverage uncertainty to resolve. If image_only substantially outperforms RNA-only, we should prioritize multimodal and image-heavy configurations; if it is comparable or worse, we can focus the remaining budget on RNA encoder upgrades (scvi, scgpt) and multiprofile aggregation. This single experiment partitions the 51-config space into two very different search strategies."
}

